{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30233 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "Angoroside-C is implicated in the targeting of Caspase-5, which is a key enzyme involved in the regulation of apoptosis. This targeting is further mediated by two distinct metabolites: 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid and Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate, both of which have been identified as targets of Angoroside-C. These metabolites, in turn, are linked to Replicase polyprotein 1ab, suggesting a potential pathway through which Angoroside-C exerts its effects. The shared involvement of Caspase-5 and the subsequent targets in the metabolic cascade indicates a possible mechanism by which Angoroside-C may influence viral replication. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Caspase-5 in the biological response to Angoroside-C, with the replicase polyprotein 1ab being a downstream effector in this process. The evidence supports a role for Angoroside-C in modulating viral replication through the Caspase-5 pathway, emphasizing the significance of this interaction in the broader context of antiviral activity.",
